"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe innocence of a family member has been proven, but rather than rejoicing, it's unpleasant and uncomfortable that chaos has returned to the once-peaceful household.  \nIt's an uncomfortable truth.  \nJacko was falsely accused, but he probably wasn't purely innocent in character.  \n\nNeither  nor  appears.\nThis book has a narrative structure closer to a family drama than a traditional mystery novel.  \n\nIt was also produced as a BBC drama, but the ending is different and the characters' psychology is different.  \nIt feels like they only took the general flow.\n"